{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>Who will declare his way to his face</b> — it returns to its place, and the sense is: who told him that his way should be so? And he does what he pleases, and there is none to requite him. And some say: that it is joined, and the sense concerns the thought of the wicked, that he does what he pleases and there is none to requite him."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:22.426464875Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}